WEBVTT

NOTE Made by video/captions.py from the film's own words (video/transcribe.py).

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.640
Every day, you capture a massive trail of information.

00:00:03.840 --> 00:00:07.740
Book highlights, margin scribbles, voice memos, and saved articles.

00:00:07.880 --> 00:00:10.660
You save all this material because you intend to use it.

00:00:10.660 --> 00:00:14.360
But months later, when it is actually time to create,

00:00:14.480 --> 00:00:17.220
those brilliant fragments are completely hidden,

00:00:17.220 --> 00:00:19.260
leaving you staring at a blank page.

00:00:19.440 --> 00:00:22.080
Our default organization creates friction.

00:00:22.080 --> 00:00:24.680
We instinctively file notes away by their source,

00:00:24.680 --> 00:00:27.540
trapping them in folders labeled by book, author, or date.

00:00:27.540 --> 00:00:30.720
Because they are locked inside impermeable walls,

00:00:30.860 --> 00:00:33.900
a history quote cannot interact with an old podcast note.

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:38.160
To make these scattered thoughts useful, the organization method has to invert.

00:00:38.340 --> 00:00:40.580
Instead of grouping notes by where they came from,

00:00:40.580 --> 00:00:43.560
they must be grouped by the actual ideas they represent.

00:00:43.720 --> 00:00:47.180
This concept-first architecture is the foundation of Marginborn.

00:00:47.540 --> 00:00:51.280
Gathering your notes by idea rather than by book is the exact mechanism

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:55.340
required to turn a static archive of quotes into a living engine of thought.

00:00:55.340 --> 00:00:59.260
Getting physical media into this environment is nearly frictionless.

00:00:59.280 --> 00:01:03.160
You simply photograph a marked passage directly from the page of a physical book.

00:01:03.460 --> 00:01:07.740
The moment that image is captured, the system runs an automated security sweep,

00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:10.540
instantly checking the text to scrub out sensitive details,

00:01:10.540 --> 00:01:12.800
like credit card numbers or email addresses.

00:01:13.080 --> 00:01:15.780
Once the text is secure, extraction begins.

00:01:15.900 --> 00:01:19.400
The text is detached from the book, and you tag it with a central concept.

00:01:19.400 --> 00:01:22.620
By tagging, you sever it from its original medium.

00:01:22.720 --> 00:01:24.280
The central node then pulses,

00:01:24.320 --> 00:01:27.620
actively searching for other notes that share that exact concept.

00:01:27.820 --> 00:01:31.340
This identical extraction pipeline works for your digital life as well.

00:01:31.400 --> 00:01:34.100
Share web links or pictures directly from other apps,

00:01:34.100 --> 00:01:35.920
routing them straight into the system.

00:01:36.040 --> 00:01:39.020
Capturing raw text accomplishes very little on its own.

00:01:39.020 --> 00:01:43.140
Assigning an immediate conceptual anchor is what makes the information usable later.

00:01:43.140 --> 00:01:49.060
All of these conceptual nodes gather in a central hub called the Commonplace view,

00:01:49.060 --> 00:01:52.040
forming an interconnected cloud of ideas.

00:01:52.240 --> 00:01:54.940
This structure collapses time completely.

00:01:55.320 --> 00:01:58.380
A note from an old podcast and a highlight from a book read

00:01:58.380 --> 00:02:02.420
yesterday snap together perfectly when they share an idea tag.

00:02:02.580 --> 00:02:07.820
Click to see related notes, and the structure expands downward, revealing the stems,

00:02:07.820 --> 00:02:10.900
exposing hidden connections between seemingly separate thoughts.

00:02:10.900 --> 00:02:14.840
You manage your custom logic inside the Lexicon.

00:02:15.120 --> 00:02:19.480
This is your personalized storage area for the unique lenses you apply to your work,

00:02:19.560 --> 00:02:23.060
your active collections, and the specific questions you are trying to answer.

00:02:23.360 --> 00:02:26.900
To keep the network healthy, the system performs active maintenance.

00:02:27.140 --> 00:02:30.760
Marginborn automatically offers to tag orphaned notes for you and

00:02:30.760 --> 00:02:33.860
regularly checks in to ask if your old questions are still open.

00:02:33.860 --> 00:02:38.900
Traditional digital folders merely hold your data in static isolation.

00:02:39.280 --> 00:02:43.360
This environment actively organizes itself around your evolving interests.

00:02:43.560 --> 00:02:46.540
This active, self-organizing network forces your past

00:02:46.540 --> 00:02:49.860
discoveries to bridge directly into your present thoughts.

00:02:50.340 --> 00:02:53.780
Months after you save a note, you sit down to start a new project.

00:02:53.820 --> 00:02:55.440
You vaguely remember a perfect quote,

00:02:55.440 --> 00:02:58.200
but you can't recall the author or the exact phrasing.

00:02:58.200 --> 00:03:00.980
A rigid keyword search fails here.

00:03:00.980 --> 00:03:05.020
Instead, Marginborn uses search by meaning, allowing you to find notes

00:03:05.020 --> 00:03:09.280
based on the intent of the idea, even if you type completely different words.

00:03:09.540 --> 00:03:12.860
When that forgotten quote surfaces exactly when you need it,

00:03:12.860 --> 00:03:16.980
you experience what Marginborn calls a braird, as seen here.

00:03:17.040 --> 00:03:19.360
It's named for the Scottish term for the first green

00:03:19.360 --> 00:03:21.960
shoots that pushed through the soil after sowing.

00:03:22.240 --> 00:03:25.200
The more notes you feed into this idea-centric structure,

00:03:25.200 --> 00:03:27.460
the stronger this return on investment becomes.

00:03:27.460 --> 00:03:29.660
Patterns, recurring questions,

00:03:29.660 --> 00:03:32.960
and larger themes reveal themselves with increasing ease.

00:03:33.180 --> 00:03:35.760
You never have to face a blank page again.

00:03:35.960 --> 00:03:37.820
Every time you sit down to work,

00:03:37.820 --> 00:03:42.120
you step into a midstream conversation with your own organized wisdom.

00:03:42.520 --> 00:03:46.040
Trusting a centralized app with your deepest personal reflections

00:03:46.040 --> 00:03:49.780
and intellectual connections requires absolute security.

00:03:49.780 --> 00:03:54.480
This is why Marginborn employs a strict cryptographic architecture.

00:03:54.880 --> 00:03:59.360
As this diagram illustrates, your personal notes and questions are locked with

00:03:59.360 --> 00:04:01.760
end-to-end encryption locally on your phone

00:04:01.760 --> 00:04:04.320
before they ever travel to the sync server.

00:04:04.480 --> 00:04:06.980
The boundaries around your data are absolute,

00:04:07.120 --> 00:04:09.980
meaning search runs entirely on your local device,

00:04:09.980 --> 00:04:12.580
and your personal thoughts are never routed into

00:04:12.580 --> 00:04:16.220
external AI training models or advertising algorithms.

00:04:16.690 --> 00:04:18.840
Absolute creative freedom is achieved when

00:04:18.840 --> 00:04:22.000
interconnected thought meets impenetrable privacy.

00:04:22.400 --> 00:04:27.280
You read broadly, write freely, and find your wisdom exactly when it counts.
